          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ganita Manjari | Grade 9 | Part II"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.11,
            0.881,
            0.133
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "13.5.1 Algebraic Methods for Solving a Pair of Linear Equations"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.135,
            0.152,
            0.399,
            0.175
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Think and Reflect"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.132,
            0.189,
            0.602,
            0.248
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Solve the puzzle and discuss your strategy with your friends. Can you determine the value represented by each shape?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.639,
            0.187,
            0.86,
            0.338
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 5,
              "bbox": [
                0.639,
                0.187,
                0.86,
                0.338
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_21_image_5.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.353,
            0.881,
            0.451
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We note from the first row that the values of 2 triangles and 2 rectangles add up to 28. We may express this as "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2T + 2R = 28"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " or as "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm{T} + \\mathrm{R} = 14"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . Similarly, the last column may be written as "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2C + T + R = 22"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Here T, S and C represent the values assigned to a triangle, a rectangle and a circle respectively."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.455,
            0.881,
            0.514
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Since we know that T + R = 14, we can rewrite the second equation as "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2C + 14 = 22"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , solving which, we get "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathbb { C } \\equiv 4 ."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . Once you have the value of C, you can find the values of the other shapes. Try it for yourself."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.517,
            0.882,
            0.576
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We will now learn two methods for solving a pair of linear equations. One is called the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "method of substitution",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " while the other is referred to as the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "method of elimination",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.581,
            0.881,
            0.621
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Substitution Method:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " We will demonstrate the method of substitution by solving a pair of linear equations in two variables."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.625,
            0.881,
            0.664
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 7:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Solve the following pair of equations by substitution method:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.418,
            0.664,
            0.879,
            0.683
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_21_equation_11.jpg",
          "content": "7x - 15y = 2\\tag{1}"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.442,
            0.69,
            0.879,
            0.71
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_21_equation_12.jpg",
          "content": "x + 2y = 3\\tag{2}"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.71,
            0.264,
            0.729
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Solution:"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.736,
            0.881,
            0.773
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Step 1:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " We select either of the equations and express one variable in terms of the other."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.774,
            0.805,
            0.793
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let us consider Equation (2), that is, x + 2y = 3 and write it as"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.43,
            0.793,
            0.879,
            0.812
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_21_equation_16.jpg",
          "content": "x = 3 - 2 y\\tag{3}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.818,
            0.881,
            0.877
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Step 2:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Clearly, all "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "( x , y )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " that satisfy both the given equations must also satisfy "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "x = 3 - 2 y"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . Since this relation must hold true in Equation (1), substituting "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "x = 3 -"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " 2y in it we get"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.403,
            0.881,
            0.597,
            0.901
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_21_equation_18.jpg",
          "content": "7(3 - 2y) - 15y = 2"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
